IfElseCircuit in ifelse_circuit.py is a port of Loom's src/loom/eka/ifelse_circuit.py
(entropicalabs/el-loom 0.4.0, https://github.com/entropicalabs/el-loom) from a pydantic
dataclass to a plain class. It follows that file's structure, fields and defaults, its messages
word for word, its string layouts and the expressions of its methods closely. That file is the
only one of the 160 Python files in el-loom 0.4.0's source distribution without the Apache
License 2.0 header (the licence of the rest, in LICENSE in this directory). In its place it
carries the following notice, kept here as it reads there:

    Copyright (c) Entropica Labs Pte Ltd 2025.

    Use, distribution and reproduction of this program in its source or compiled
    form is prohibited without the express written consent of Entropica Labs Pte
    Ltd.

On 2026-10-21 the file on el-loom's main branch carried the same notice, and PyPI had no
release later than 0.4.0. No consent of Entropica Labs Pte Ltd to this port has been obtained,
so whether IfElseCircuit may be distributed, and under what licence, is unresolved.
